      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "*** HIGH LEVEL DESIGN ***",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "*** HIGH LEVEL DESIGN ***",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "6V3EFUQRgNsTVXfU3uqsV",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 419,
      "y": 518.5,
      "width": 95.07989501953125,
      "height": 25,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#e03131",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b7R",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1951906565,
      "version": 14,
      "versionNonce": 272057061,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1787263806542,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Principles:",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Principles:",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "tpadMe3hbIq75a60O_Gpf",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 416.9296875,
      "y": 559.85546875,
      "width": 638.9014892578125,
      "height": 625,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b7T",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1220804293,
      "version": 121,
      "versionNonce": 1316970725,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1787263865877,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1) Cache immutable versions, not mutable results.\nEvery materialization is keyed by the exact versions of its\ndependencies.\n\n2) Use DAG lineage for precise invalidation.\nA change only dirties affected descendants and partitions.\n\n3) Prefer incremental and partition-level updates.\nA late update for one day should not recompute years of\nhistory.\n\n4) Separate computation from publication.\nBuild → persist → validate → atomically publish.\n\n5) Make consistency a query-level SLA.\nStrong queries wait for compatible latest snapshots; dashboards\nmay accept bounded staleness.\n\n6) Use multi-tier caching based on reuse and recomputation cost.\nRAM for very hot data, SSD for larger reusable blocks, shared\ncache for fleet reuse.\n\n7) Protect the cache from workloads, not just capacity limits.\nTinyLFU/admission control, tenant quotas, single-flight, hot-key\nreplication, and priority-aware backfills prevent thrashing.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1) Cache immutable versions, not mutable results.\nEvery materialization is keyed by the exact versions of its dependencies.\n\n2) Use DAG lineage for precise invalidation.\nA change only dirties affected descendants and partitions.\n\n3) Prefer incremental and partition-level updates.\nA late update for one day should not recompute years of history.\n\n4) Separate computation from publication.\nBuild → persist → validate → atomically publish.\n\n5) Make consistency a query-level SLA.\nStrong queries wait for compatible latest snapshots; dashboards may accept bounded staleness.\n\n6) Use multi-tier caching based on reuse and recomputation cost.\nRAM for very hot data, SSD for larger reusable blocks, shared cache for fleet reuse.\n\n7) Protect the cache from workloads, not just capacity limits.\nTinyLFU/admission control, tenant quotas, single-flight, hot-key replication, and priority-aware backfills prevent thrashing.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
